[31m-[m
[31m-## Overview[m
[31m-[m
[31m-This project implements a four-way traffic light controller for North, South, East, and West directions. The controller uses an FSM to manage traffic signal transitions, generate timing intervals, and handle emergency requests.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The design was developed in Verilog HDL, simulated using Icarus Verilog, and analyzed using AMD/Xilinx Vivado. The hardware implementation targets the Digilent Basys 3 FPGA board.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Key Features[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- Four-way traffic signal control.[m
[31m-- FSM-based RTL design.[m
[31m-- Internal one-second timing generation from the FPGA clock.[m
[31m-- Configurable green, yellow, all-red, and emergency timings.[m
[31m-- Manual emergency request inputs for all four directions.[m
[31m-- Fixed emergency priority: **North > South > East > West**.[m
[31m-- Safe ALL-RED transitions before emergency green.[m
[31m-- Handling of multiple simultaneous emergency requests.[m
[31m-- Verilog testbench and simulation waveform.[m
[31m-- Vivado RTL, synthesis, and implementation analysis.[m
[31m-- Basys 3 XDC constraints and generated FPGA bitstream.[m
[31m-- Hardware implementation evidence.[m
[31m-[m
