[31m-## System Architecture[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The system consists of the following functional components:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-1. **Clock and timing logic:** Generates the one-second timing event used by the FSM.[m
[31m-2. **Traffic controller FSM:** Controls normal traffic sequencing and emergency states.[m
[31m-3. **Emergency priority logic:** Selects the highest-priority active emergency request.[m
[31m-4. **Traffic signal outputs:** Drive the red, yellow, and green indicators for all four directions.[m
[31m-5. **FPGA interface:** Connects the controller to the Basys 3 clock, reset, switches, and LEDs through the XDC constraints.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Normal Traffic Sequence[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The controller follows this repeating sequence:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-1. North and South GREEN; East and West RED.[m
[31m-2. North and South YELLOW; East and West RED.[m
[31m-3. ALL RED.[m
[31m-4. East and West GREEN; North and South RED.[m
[31m-5. East and West YELLOW; North and South RED.[m
[31m-6. ALL RED.[m
[31m-7. Repeat.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The all-red intervals separate conflicting traffic movements.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Emergency Priority System[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The controller accepts four manual emergency request inputs:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-| Input | Direction |[m
[31m-|---|---|[m
[31m-| `emergency_north` | North |[m
[31m-| `emergency_south` | South |[m
[31m-| `emergency_east` | East |[m
[31m-| `emergency_west` | West |[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The priority order is:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**North > South > East > West**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-When an emergency request is selected at a designated all-red transition, the controller grants the selected direction a green signal while keeping conflicting directions red. Multiple simultaneous requests are resolved according to the fixed priority order.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Emergency requests are represented by FPGA input signals; physical emergency vehicle detection sensors are not part of this version.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Timing Configuration[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The intended default parameters are:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-| Parameter | Value |[m
[31m-|---|---:|[m
[31m-| `CLK_FREQ` | 100,000,000 Hz |[m
[31m-| `GREEN_TIME` | 10 seconds |[m
[31m-| `YELLOW_TIME` | 3 seconds |[m
[31m-| `ALL_RED_TIME` | 1 second |[m
[31m-| `EMERGENCY_TIME` | 10 seconds |[m
[31m-[m
[31m-These parameters are defined in the RTL design and can be adjusted for supported configurations.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Hardware Implementation[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The controller targets the **Digilent Basys 3 FPGA development board**.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The hardware interface uses:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- The onboard 100 MHz clock.[m
[31m-- A push button for reset.[m
[31m-- Four slide switches for emergency requests.[m
[31m-- LEDs for the traffic signal outputs.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The XDC file defines the FPGA pin assignments and I/O standards. The generated bitstream can be used to configure the FPGA with the corresponding implemented design.[m
